1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,300
2,291 pieces of jade. One body.
2291块玉，拼成一个人

2
00:00:02,300 --> 00:00:04,600
Every other jade suit used gold wire.
别处的玉衣都用金丝穿

3
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:06,900
This king chose silk — red silk.
这位王偏用红丝线

4
00:00:06,900 --> 00:00:09,200
The only silk-sewn jade suit on Earth.
全世界唯一的丝缕玉衣

5
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:11,500
Buried in Guangzhou for 2,000 years.
在广州地下埋了两千年

6
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:13,800
Its king: Zhao Mo of Nanyue.
南越第二代王 · 赵眜

7
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:16,100
Found by accident in 1983.
1983年 意外重见天日

8
00:00:16,100 --> 00:00:18,400
The silk? Still red after 20 centuries.
那丝线 · 两千年后仍是红的

9
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:20,900
★ Expert Tip: see it at Nanyue King Museum, free-ish and quiet.
内行提示：南越王博物院看真身

10
00:00:20,900 --> 00:00:23,500
Buried in jade, or in gold — which would you pick?
你选玉衣还是金缕？评论区见
